{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q8D8MXxnYXFeAAKCARcAhJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# manigot web UI\n2\t\n3\tThe control-plane client for `mg serve` — a Svelte 5 single-page app that\n4\trenders the daemon's read-only API today and the mutating surface as it lands.\n5\tIt is a port of the TUI's information design: same data, same job pipeline,\n6\tsame attention ordering — built for a browser, so the \"review from a phone,\n7\tget a ping when a job needs you, act on it\" story has a surface.\n8\t\n9\t## Running\n10\t\n11\t```sh\n12\tnpm install\n13\tnpm run dev        # vite dev server on :5173\n14\tnpm run dev:mock   # same, with the in-browser mock daemon (no mg serve needed)\n15\tnpm run build      # production build to dist/\n16\tnpm run test       # vitest suite\n17\t```\n18\t\n19\tThe app talks to the daemon through the connection setting (Settings modal /\n20\t`?api=` URL param). The daemon is a same-origin JSON API — it sends no CORS\n21\theaders, so the browser blocks any direct cross-origin URL (the error will\n22\tsay \"cross-origin URL blocked\"). In dev, use the vite proxy path instead:\n23\t\n24\t```sh\n25\tnpm run dev\n26\t# open http://localhost:5173/?api=/api\n27\t```\n28\t\n29\t`/api` is same-origin (vite proxies it to `127.0.0.1:8080`, forwarding the\n30\tbearer token). Served by the daemon itself (production, same origin) there\n31\tis nothing to configure; against a remote daemon behind a reverse proxy the\n32\tproxy serves both the UI and `/api`. For a non-loopback daemon bind, set the\n33\tbearer token in the settings modal (`mg serve-token` writes one to the\n34\tdaemon's `.env` — tokens never ride in URLs).\n35\t\n36\tDevelopment conveniences:\n37\t\n38\t- `?api=<url>` — point the session at a daemon without touching settings\n39\t  (deep-link/testing only; tokens stay in the settings modal).\n40\t- `?mock=1` (or `--mode mock`) — swap the API layer for the in-browser\n41\t  fixture backend (`src/lib/api/mock.ts`), so the UI is fully explorable with\n42\t  no daemon running. The mock mirrors the real API shapes exactly — its\n43\t  routes are pinned by `mock.test.ts` so the dev environment cannot silently\n44\t  drift from the shipped daemon.\n45\t\n46\t## Layout\n47\t\n48\t```\n49\tsrc/\n50\t  App.svelte            shell: rail, router, connection bar, palette\n51\t  main.ts               bootstrap\n52\t  lib/\n53\t    api/                client, endpoint paths, types, mock backend, SSE stream\n54\t    components/         Pipeline, MarkdownView, DiffView, RunConsole, modals, …\n55\t    state/              connection, data (polling), toasts stores\n56\t    views/              JobsView, JobDetailView, AgentsView, HealthView\n57\t    diff.ts             parse git log/stat/patch into renderable structures\n58\t    runlog.ts           parse run.log event timeline (incl. NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT)\n59\t    markdown.ts         sanitized markdown render + verdict/status extraction\n60\t    stage.ts            pipeline stage ordering + attention sorting\n61\t    router.ts           hash router (#/p/<project>[/j/<job>[/<tab>]])\n62\t    time.ts             relative time formatting\n63\t```\n64\t\n65\t## Design notes\n66\t\n67\t- **Part 1 / Part 2 capability probing** — the client treats a 404/405 from a\n68\t  mutating endpoint as a *capability miss* (`ApiError.capabilityMiss`), so\n69\t  the same frontend runs against a read-only daemon (actions greyed out with\n70\t  an explanation) and against the full control plane once job two's endpoints\n71\t  land.\n72\t- **Attention-first job list** — `stopped:needs-human` outranks `running`\n73\t  outranks quiet; the segmented filter and the sort share one `stage.ts`.\n74\t- **Live run console** — the Run tab polls `/jdi` for the event timeline and\n75\t  attaches the `session.log` stream over SSE when the daemon offers it,\n76\t  degrading to polling otherwise; the mode is shown, never hidden.\n77\t- **Job files** — the daemon serves job files by their on-disk name\n78\t  (`brief.md`, not `brief`); the client maps tab ids to filenames.\n79\t- **Accessibility** — WCAG AA contrast on all informative text, keyboard\n80\t  navigation throughout, ARIA roles on interactive affordances, verified per\n81\t  render with the `shot` tool at 375/768/1280."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"561e42e9-f91a-46b3-ab07-d4e54ed01e9c","uuid":"18ae2c83-a72d-4eba-aab1-692f6e0b847b","timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:59:36.790Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/web-ui/README.md","content":"# manigot web UI\n\nThe control-plane client for `mg serve` — a Svelte 5 single-page app that\nrenders the daemon's read-only API today and the mutating surface as it lands.\nIt is a port of the TUI's information design: same data, same job pipeline,\nsame attention ordering — built for a browser, so the \"review from a phone,\nget a ping when a job needs you, act on it\" story has a surface.\n\n## Running\n\n```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run dev        # vite dev server on :5173\nnpm run dev:mock   # same, with the in-browser mock daemon (no mg serve needed)\nnpm run build      # production build to dist/\nnpm run test       # vitest suite\n```\n\nThe app talks to the daemon through the connection setting (Settings modal /\n`?api=` URL param). The daemon is a same-origin JSON API — it sends no CORS\nheaders, so the browser blocks any direct cross-origin URL (the error will\nsay \"cross-origin URL blocked\"). In dev, use the vite proxy path instead:\n\n```sh\nnpm run dev\n# open http://localhost:5173/?api=/api\n```\n\n`/api` is same-origin (vite proxies it to `127.0.0.1:8080`, forwarding the\nbearer token). Served by the daemon itself (production, same origin) there\nis nothing to configure; against a remote daemon behind a reverse proxy the\nproxy serves both the UI and `/api`. For a non-loopback daemon bind, set the\nbearer token in the settings modal (`mg serve-token` writes one to the\ndaemon's `.env` — tokens never ride in URLs).\n\nDevelopment conveniences:\n\n- `?api=<url>` — point the session at a daemon without touching settings\n  (deep-link/testing only; tokens stay in the settings modal).\n- `?mock=1` (or `--mode mock`) — swap the API layer for the in-browser\n  fixture backend (`src/lib/api/mock.ts`), so the UI is fully explorable with\n  no daemon running. The mock mirrors the real API shapes exactly — its\n  routes are pinned by `mock.test.ts` so the dev environment cannot silently\n  drift from the shipped daemon.\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nsrc/\n  App.svelte            shell: rail, router, connection bar, palette\n  main.ts               bootstrap\n  lib/\n    api/                client, endpoint paths, types, mock backend, SSE stream\n    components/         Pipeline, MarkdownView, DiffView, RunConsole, modals, …\n    state/              connection, data (polling), toasts stores\n    views/              JobsView, JobDetailView, AgentsView, HealthView\n    diff.ts             parse git log/stat/patch into renderable structures\n    runlog.ts           parse run.log event timeline (incl. NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT)\n    markdown.ts         sanitized markdown render + verdict/status extraction\n    stage.ts            pipeline stage ordering + attention sorting\n    router.ts           hash router (#/p/<project>[/j/<job>[/<tab>]])\n    time.ts             relative time formatting\n```\n\n## Design notes\n\n- **Part 1 / Part 2 capability probing** — the client treats a 404/405 from a\n  mutating endpoint as a *capability miss* (`ApiError.capabilityMiss`), so\n  the same frontend runs against a read-only daemon (actions greyed out with\n  an explanation) and against the full control plane once job two's endpoints\n  land.\n- **Attention-first job list** — `stopped:needs-human` outranks `running`\n  outranks quiet; the segmented filter and the sort share one `stage.ts`.\n- **Live run console** — the Run tab polls `/jdi` for the event timeline and\n  attaches the `session.log` stream over SSE when the daemon offers it,\n  degrading to polling otherwise; the mode is shown, never hidden.\n- **Job files** — the daemon serves job files by their on-disk name\n  (`brief.md`, not `brief`); the client maps tab ids to filenames.\n- **Accessibility** — WCAG AA contrast on all informative text, keyboard\n  navigation throughout, ARIA roles on interactive affordances, verified per\n  render with the `shot` tool at 375/768/1280.","numLines":81,"startLine":1,"totalLines":81}}}
